# 🕸️ Coffee Quality Data Scraping

This folder contains all scripts and resources used to scrape coffee quality data from the Coffee Quality Institute (CQI) website.

The scraping workflow is isolated from the rest of the project using a dedicated virtual environment.

---

## 📂 Folder Structure

scraped_dataset/
├── .venv/ # Virtual environment for scraping
├── requirements.txt # Scraper dependencies
├── scraper/
│ ├── scraper_bot.py # Main Selenium scraper
│ ├── moving_csv.py # Moves generated CSV files to raw_data/
│ ├── process_tables_f.py # Combines tables into one dataset
│ ├── raw_data/ # Raw scraped CSV files
│ └── df_1_arabica.csv # Combined dataset (un-cleaned)


---

## 🔐 Authentication

The CQI website requires user authentication to access coffee quality data.

The scraper:
1. Opens the CQI login page
2. Submits user credentials
3. Navigates to the Arabica coffees listing

> Credentials are **not committed** to this repository.

---

## 🛠️ Environment Setup

```bash
python -m venv .venv
.\.venv\Scripts\activate
pip install -r requirements.txt

🧪 Scraping Process
The scraper navigates to the Arabica coffees section
Iterates through all available pages (5 pages total)
Opens each coffee detail page
Extracts all HTML tables
Saves tables as individual CSV files
Each coffee generates multiple CSV files named: coffee_<coffee_id>_table_<table_id>.csv 

📦 Raw Data Organization
After scraping, moving_csv.py:
Creates a raw_data/ folder
Moves all generated CSV files into it

🔗 Table Processing
process_tables_f.py:
Reads tables from raw_data/
Merges tables belonging to the same coffee
Skips incomplete entries
Outputs: df_1_arabica.csv
